{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Do you intend to prove words?</b> — Actual words, with which you could prove. The meaning is that you have no proof." "<b>And to the wind</b> — And furthermore: that you consider the words of a despairing man to be wind. The meaning is that you think your words are sound, and the words of one who is in suffering — vanity."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:09.303764506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}